   PCA is a graph-by-graph method that reduces the dimensionality of the data while preserving as much information as possible. The algorithm finds linear combinations of the original variables (temperature, humidity, pH) that explain the most variation in the data. These linear combinations are called principal axes, and the first axis (P1) explains the most variation, the second axis (P2) explains the second most, and so on.  

