","To find the mass of sodium fluoride in a 10 mL dose, we can use the following formula:  
\[ \text{Mass} = \text{Concentration} \times \text{Volume} \]  

Given:  
- Concentration = 0.044% (w/v) = 0.044 g/100 mL  
- Volume = 10 mL  

Substitute the values into the formula:  
\[ \text{Mass} = \left( \frac{0.044 \text{ g}}{100 \text{ mL}} \right) \times 10 \text{ mL} \]  
\[ \text{Mass} = 0.0044 \text{ g} \]  

Convert the mass from grams to milligrams:  
\[ \text{Mass} = 0.0044 \text{ g} \times \frac{1000 \text{ mg}}{1 \text{ g}} \]  
\[ \text{Mass} = 4.4 \text{ mg} \]  

Thus, there are \(\boxed{4.4 \text{ mg}}\) of sodium fluoride in a 10 mL dose of Phos-Flur Rinse.
