Now, we need to determine the number of moles of electrons (n) transferred in the reaction. In this case, one mole of electrons is transferred from Zn to Cu2+ to form Zn2+ and Cu. So, n = 1.

Now we can calculate the Gibbs free energy change:

ΔG° = -nFE°
