   \[
   \text{Moles of oxygen} = \frac{57.5 \text{ g}}{32 \text{ g/mol}} = 1.73 \text{ mol}
   \]

3. **Calculate the weight of sulphur required:**
   \[
   \text{Moles of sulphur} = \text{Moles of oxygen} = 1.73 \text{ mol}
   \]
   \[
   \text{Weight of sulphur} = 1.73 \text{ mol} \times 32 \text{ g/mol} = 53.4 \text{ g}
   \]

4. **Calculate the weight of residual gases:**
   \[
   \text{Weight of residual gases} = 250 \text{ g} - 57.5 \text{ g} - 53.4 \text{ g} = 133.1 \text{ g}
   \]

**Final Answer:**
- The amount of sulphur required is \(\boxed{53.4 \text{ g}}\).
