","The third law of thermodynamics states that the entropy of a perfectly-ordered crystal approaches zero as the temperature approaches absolute zero. This implies that the entropy of imperfect crystals at absolute zero would be greater than zero. This is because imperfect crystals have defects, such as impurities, vacancies, or dislocations, which introduce disorder and thus increase entropy. 

