","The Fisher esterification reaction is a nucleophilic acyl substitution reaction that converts a carboxylic acid and an alcohol into an ester, with the elimination of water as a byproduct. The reaction is catalyzed by an acid, such as sulfuric acid or hydrochloric acid. The general reaction is as follows:

\[
\text{RCOOH} + \text{R}_2\text{OH} \rightleftharpoons \text{RCOOR}_2 + \text{H}_2\text{O}
