   \]

2. **Calculate the relative speed of the train relative to the jogger**:  
   \[
   12 \, \text{m/s} - 9 \, \text{m/s} = 3 \, \text{m/s}
   \]

3. **Determine the length of the train**:  
   The time \( t = 25 \, \text{s} \) is the time it takes the train to cover the distance equal to its length plus the 150 m distance it was away from the jogger. The relative speed \( 3 \, \text{m/s} \) is used here because the jogger is moving in the same direction.  
   \[
   \text{Length of train} + 150 \, \text{m} = \text{relative speed} \times t = 3 \, \text{m/s} \times 25 \, \text{s} = 75 \, \text{m}
   \]  
   \[
   \text{Length of train} = 75 \, \text{m} - 150 \, \text{m} = -75 \, \text{m}
   \]

4. **Interpret the result**:  
   The negative value indicates that the jogger is not 150 m ahead of the train, but that the train is 150 m behind the jogger.  

