- \( d \) is the separation between the slits (1 mm = \( 10^{-3} \) m, so \( d = \frac{1}{800} \times 10^{-3} \) m),
- \( \theta \) is the angle between the central maximum and the maximum of order \( n \),
- \( n \) is the order of the maximum (3 in this case).

Rearranging the formula to solve for \( \theta \):

\[
\sin \theta = \frac{n \lambda}{d}
\]

\[
\theta = \sin^{-1} \left( \frac{n \lambda}{d} \right)
\]

