In summary, the method involves:
1. Measuring the cross section for electron-posittron scattering at high energies.
2. Using the Dyan-type perturbation theory to calculate the cross section in terms of the strong coupling constant.
3. Fitting the experimental cross section data to the theoretical prediction to determine the value of α_s.

This method is particularly precise because it involves the measurement of a well-defined observable (the cross section) and the use of a well-accurate theoretical framework.
