   - **Mermerges**: The most abundant sources are mergers of electron-electron pairs, which are predicted to occur at a rate of $\boxed{10^6 \text{ per year}}$ in the habitable zone of a 100-km-radius area.
   - **Other Sources**: Other sources like planetary orbits, planetary rotations, and even cosmic defects (e.g., magnetic monopoles) are expected to produce detectable gravitational waves, but at much lower rates.

