2. **Solidparticle Reinforcement**: The presence of these hard particles also reduces the percent elongation of the alloy. As the alloy is subjected to stress, the dislocation movement becomes more difficult due to the presence of the particles. This makes it more difficult for the material to deform and elongate before breaking, leading to a lower percent elongation.

