     \[ \text{N}_2\text{O}_4 \rightleftharpoons 2\text{NO}_2. \]  
   - At equilibrium, the total molar mass of the gas is:  
     \[ \text{Molar mass at equilibrium} = \text{Molar mass of N}_2\text{O}_4 \times (1 - \alpha) + \text{Molar mass of NO}_2 \times 2\alpha. \]  
   - Substituting the molar masses:  
     \[ 51.34 = 98.02 \times (1 - \alpha) + 46 \times 2\alpha. \]  
